## 🔴 SECTION 1: SYSADMIN FLOW

### How Sysadmin Auth Works
```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Sysadmin credentials stored in .env file:                │
│   SYSADMIN_EMAIL=admin@system.com                        │
│   SYSADMIN_PASSWORD=hashed_password_here                 │
│                                                          │
│ POST /api/sysadmin/login                                 │
│   → Compare email + bcrypt compare password from .env   │
│   → If match → generate JWT with { id: 'sysadmin',      │
│                role: 'sysadmin' }                        │
│   → Set JWT in HttpOnly cookie 'token'                   │
│   → If not → return 401                                  │
│                                                          │
│ POST /api/sysadmin/logout                                │
│   → Clear 'token' cookie                                 │
│                                                          │
│ All sysadmin routes: authenticate → requireRole('sysadmin') │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Sysadmin Endpoints (9 total)
| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| POST | /api/sysadmin/login | Sysadmin login |
| POST | /api/sysadmin/logout | Sysadmin logout |
| POST | /api/sysadmin/create_new_college | Create college + first admin user (transaction) |
| GET | /api/sysadmin/get_all_colleges | List all colleges (paginated) |
| GET | /api/sysadmin/get_college/:collegeId | Get college details |
| PUT | /api/sysadmin/update_college/:collegeId | Update college info |
| PATCH | /api/sysadmin/toggle_college_status/:collegeId | Activate/deactivate college |
| PATCH | /api/sysadmin/update_college_features/:collegeId | Update enabled features |
| PATCH | /api/sysadmin/update_academic_year/:collegeId | Update default academic year |

### Flow: Creating a College

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant SA as Sysadmin
    participant API as Backend
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    SA->>API: POST /api/sysadmin/create_new_college
    Note right of API: Body: college_name, subdomain,<br/>address, type, academic_year,<br/>admin_email, admin_password

    API->>API: Validate input (Joi)
    API->>DB: Check subdomain uniqueness
    DB-->>API: No duplicate found

    API->>API: Hash admin password (bcrypt, 10 rounds)

    API->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    API->>DB: INSERT into colleges table
    DB-->>API: college_id returned

    API->>DB: INSERT into users table<br/>(college_id, admin_email, hashed_password,<br/>user_role='collegeadmin')
    DB-->>API: user_id returned

    API->>DB: COMMIT
    API-->>SA: { success: true, data: { college, adminUser } }
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **When creating a college, also create the first college admin user** in a single transaction. This ensures a valid login always exists for every college in the system.

