## 🟢 SECTION 2: COLLEGE ADMIN FLOW

### College User Roles
| Role | DB value | Who they are |
|------|----------|-------------|
| College Admin | `collegeadmin` | Created by sysadmin. Full admin access. |
| TPO | `tpo` | Training & Placement Officer. Manages placements. |
| TPC | `tpc` | Training & Placement Coordinator. Similar to TPO. |
| HOD | `hod` | Head of Department. Department-scoped access. |
| Teacher | `teacher` | Faculty member. Limited access. |

> [!NOTE]
> `tpc` role was added to the `users_role_check` DB constraint. All five non-sysadmin roles are valid: `collegeadmin`, `tpo`, `tpc`, `hod`, `teacher`.

### College User Endpoints (9 total)
| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|------|-------------|
| POST | /api/college/login | public + authLimiter | College user login |
| POST | /api/college/logout | authenticate | Logout (clear cookie) |
| POST | /api/college/forgot_password | public + authLimiter | Send reset email |
| POST | /api/college/reset_password | public + authLimiter | Reset password from email link token |
| POST | /api/college/change_password | authenticate | Change own password |
| POST | /api/college/create_user | authenticate + requireRole(collegeadmin) | Create new college user |
| GET | /api/college/get_all_users | authenticate + requireRole(collegeadmin) | List all users (paginated, filterable) |
| GET | /api/college/get_user/:userId | authenticate + requireRole(collegeadmin) | Get user details |
| PUT | /api/college/update_user/:userId | authenticate + requireRole(collegeadmin) | Update user |
| PATCH | /api/college/toggle_user_status/:userId | authenticate + requireRole(collegeadmin) | Activate/deactivate user |

### College User Login Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as College User
    participant API as Backend
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    U->>API: POST /api/college/login
    Note right of API: Body: email, password

    API->>DB: SELECT user + college WHERE LOWER(user_email) = LOWER($1)
    DB-->>API: User record found

    API->>API: Check college.college_status === 'active'
    Note over API: If inactive → 403

    API->>API: Check user.user_status === 'active'
    Note over API: If inactive → 403

    API->>API: bcrypt.compare(password, user.user_password)
    Note over API: If wrong → 401

    API->>API: generateToken({ id: user_id, college_id, role: user_role })
    API->>API: Set JWT in HttpOnly cookie 'token'

    API-->>U: { user: { user_id, user_name, user_role, college_name, ... } }
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> JWT Payload: `{ id: user_id, college_id, role }`. The `college_id` is used in EVERY subsequent query for data isolation.

### Forgot Password / Reset Password Flow

```
FORGOT PASSWORD:
1. POST /api/college/forgot_password → { email }
2. Find user by email (email enumeration prevented — always return same message)
3. Generate reset JWT: { id: user_id, purpose: 'password_reset' } with 15 min expiry
4. Send email with link: ${FRONTEND_URL}/reset-password?token=<jwt>
5. Return 200 with generic success message (never reveal whether email exists)

RESET PASSWORD:
1. POST /api/college/reset_password → { token, new_password, confirm_password }
2. verifyToken(token) — checks JWT signature + expiry
3. Validate payload: payload.purpose === 'password_reset'
4. Find user by payload.id in users table
5. Hash new password, UPDATE users SET user_password = $1
6. Return success — user must now log in fresh
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Token is a **stateless JWT** (no DB storage, no Redis needed). The 15-minute expiry is enforced by JWT signature verification. A used token remains technically valid until expiry — this implementation assumes the frontend redirects away after use.

