## 🔵 SECTION 3: STUDENT FLOW

### Student Auth Endpoints (5 total)
| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|------|-------------|
| POST | /api/student/login | public + authLimiter | Student login |
| POST | /api/student/logout | authenticate | Logout (clear cookie) |
| POST | /api/student/forgot_password | public + authLimiter | Send reset email |
| POST | /api/student/reset_password | public + authLimiter | Reset password from email link token |
| POST | /api/student/change_password | authenticate | Change own password |

### Student Login Flow
```
1. POST /api/student/login → { email, password }
2. SELECT student JOIN colleges WHERE LOWER(student_email) = LOWER($1)
3. Check college.college_status === 'active' → 403 if not
4. Check student.student_status === 'active' → 403 if not
5. bcrypt.compare(password, student.student_password) → 401 if wrong
6. generateToken({ id: student_id, college_id, role: 'student' })
7. Set JWT in HttpOnly cookie 'token'
8. Return student profile data (no password field)
```

### Student Forgot/Reset Password Flow
```
FORGOT:
  POST /api/student/forgot_password → { email }
  → Token payload: { id: student_id, purpose: 'password_reset', type: 'student' }
  → Email link: ${FRONTEND_URL}/student/reset-password?token=<jwt>

RESET:
  POST /api/student/reset_password → { token, new_password, confirm_password }
  → verifyToken(token): checks signature + expiry
  → Validates payload.purpose === 'password_reset' AND payload.type === 'student'
     (the 'type' check prevents college reset tokens from working on student endpoint)
  → SELECT from students WHERE student_id = payload.id
  → Hash new password, UPDATE students SET student_password = $1
```

### Student First Login & Profile Setup

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Student Registered by College Admin] --> B[Login with email + default password]
    B --> C[Change Password on First Login]
    C --> D[Profile Dashboard - Empty]
    D --> E[Fill Personal Information]
    D --> F[Fill Academic Information]
    D --> G[Add Semester Grades]
    D --> H[Add Skills]
    D --> I[Add Projects]
    D --> J[Add Experience]
    D --> K[Add Achievements & Certificates]
    D --> L[Add Profile Links]

    E & F & G & H --> M{All required sections filled?}
    M -->|Yes| N[Student sets profile_complete = true]
    N --> O[Admin Reviews Full Profile]
    O -->|Approved| P[profile_is_approved = true]
    O -->|Rejected| Q[Student updates & resubmits]
    P --> R[Can apply for jobs]
```

### Profile Completion Logic

```js
// GET /api/student/profile/completion
// Checks presence of data across multiple tables (parallel queries for performance)

const completionWeights = {
  personal_info:   20,  // student_personal_info table
  academic_info:   20,  // student_academic_info table
  semester_grades: 15,  // student_semester_grades table (at least 1 row)
  skills:          15,  // student_skills table (at least 1 skill)
  profile_links:   10,  // student_profile_links table
  projects:        10,  // student_projects table (at least 1)
  experience:       5,  // student_experience table
  certificates:     5,  // student_certificates table
};

// Returns: { percentage: 85, missing: ['experience'], sections: { ... } }
// All 8 section checks run as Promise.all() in parallel
```

### Student Profile Sections
| Section | Table | Max Items | Notes |
|---------|-------|-----------|-------|
| Personal | student_personal_info | 1 | DOB, gender, phone, address, aadhaar (never returned in API) |
| Academic | student_academic_info | 1 | 10th, 12th, entrance exam scores |
| Semester grades | student_semester_grades | per program | CGPA per semester |
| Skills | student_skills | unlimited | Links to skills master catalog |
| Projects | student_projects | max 10 | Title, description, tech stack, URL |
| Experience | student_experience | max 10 | Company, role, duration |
| Achievements | student_achievements | max 10 | Awards, competitions |
| Certificates | student_certificates | max 15 | Course name, issuer, URL |
| Activities | student_activities | max 10 | Clubs, volunteering |
| Profile links | student_profile_links | 1 | LinkedIn, GitHub, portfolio |

### Student Job Application Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant S as Student
    participant API as Backend
    participant DB as Database

    S->>API: GET /api/student/jobs (browse published jobs)
    API->>DB: SELECT jobs WHERE status='published'<br/>AND application_deadline > NOW()
    DB-->>API: List of jobs (with position_count, total_applications as aggregates)
    API-->>S: Available jobs

    S->>API: GET /api/student/jobs/:jobId/check_eligibility
    API->>DB: [parallel] verifyJob + getStudentProfile + getEligibilityCriteria
    API->>API: Run eligibility checks + checkApplicationBlockers
    API-->>S: { eligible, reasons, blockers }

    S->>API: POST /api/student/jobs/:jobId/apply
    API->>API: Verify: profile_is_approved = true
    API->>API: Verify: student passes eligibility OR has approved override
    API->>API: Verify: no active bar_from_placements restriction
    API->>API: Verify: deadline not passed
    API->>API: Verify: not already applied
    API->>DB: INSERT student_applications + INSERT application_answers (batch)
    API-->>S: { application_id, application_status: 'pending' }
```

> [!WARNING]
> **All application blockers run as parallel queries (Promise.all) before insert:**
> 1. `profile_is_approved = true`
> 2. Student passes all eligibility criteria (or has approved override)
> 3. No active `bar_from_placements` or `temporary_suspension` restriction
> 4. Application deadline has not passed
> 5. Student has not already applied to this job
> 6. Job status is `published`

### Student application answers are bulk-inserted
```js
// Instead of one INSERT per answer, answers are inserted as a single multi-row INSERT:
const values = answers.map((_, i) => `($${i*3+1}, $${i*3+2}, $${i*3+3})`).join(', ');
await query(
  `INSERT INTO application_answers (application_id, question_id, answer_text) VALUES ${values}`,
  answers.flatMap(a => [applicationId, a.question_id, a.answer_text])
);
```

