```js
// GET /api/student/my_applications
// Returns list with round results nested per application

[
  {
    application_id: "...",
    company_name: "TCS",
    company_industry: "Information Technology",  // field is 'industry_type' in API response
    job_title: "Software Developer",
    applied_at: "2025-01-15",
    application_status: "in_progress",   // pending | in_progress | shortlisted | selected | rejected | withdrawn
    rounds: [
      { round_name: "Aptitude",  round_type: "written", status: "passed",  marks: 78 },
      { round_name: "Technical", round_type: "technical", status: "passed", marks: 85 },
      { round_name: "HR",        round_type: "hr",       status: "pending" }
    ]
  }
]

// Additional endpoints:
// GET  /api/student/jobs/:jobId/my_application  — Single application details
// POST /api/student/jobs/:jobId/deny            — Opt-out of a job (eligible but choosing not to apply)
// POST /api/student/applications/:id/withdraw   — Withdraw a submitted application
```

### Placement Accept/Reject

```
Student gets offer  → GET  /api/student/my_placements
Student accepts     → PATCH /api/student/placements/:id/accept
Student rejects     → PATCH /api/student/placements/:id/reject

// On REJECT:
// 1. UPDATE placement_results SET placement_status = 'rejected'
// 2. Check placement policies — does rejecting trigger a restriction?
//    (e.g., policy: "backing out after accepting = bar_from_placements")
// 3. If policy triggered → auto-create row in student_restrictions

// On ACCEPT:
// 1. UPDATE placement_results SET placement_status = 'accepted'
// 2. Check if max_placements policy threshold reached
//    → If reached → block further placement for this student
```

### Feedback & Interview Questions

```
// After placement drive is complete, student can submit feedback:
POST /api/student/feedback
Body: { job_id, company_id, rating: 4, feedback_text: "Great process, transparent rounds." }
// → is_approved = false by default → college admin reviews + approves
// → Admin endpoint: PATCH /api/college/feedback/:id/approve OR reject

// Student shares interview questions for next batches:
POST /api/student/interview_questions
Body: {
  company_id, job_id,
  question_description: "Given an array, find two numbers that sum to target",
  topic: "Arrays",
  sample_answer: "Use HashMap approach, O(n) time..."
}
// → is_approved = false → admin approves → visible to future students
// → Browse approved Q&A: GET /api/student/interview_questions?company_id=xxx

// College admin endpoints:
GET   /api/college/feedback                     — List all feedback
PATCH /api/college/feedback/:id/approve         — Approve feedback
PATCH /api/college/feedback/:id/reject          — Reject feedback
GET   /api/college/interview_questions          — List all Q&A
PATCH /api/college/interview_questions/:id/approve  — Approve Q&A
```

