## 🛡️ Security Checklist

- [x] All passwords hashed with bcrypt (10 rounds)
- [x] JWT secret stored in .env (never in code)
- [x] JWT expiry set (7d for users/students, 15m for reset tokens)
- [x] JWT delivered via HttpOnly cookie (not Authorization header)
- [x] Rate limiting: `authLimiter` on login/forgot/reset, `apiLimiter` on writes
- [x] CORS configured with credentials support
- [x] Helmet.js security headers
- [x] Input validation on every route (Joi → 422 on failure)
- [x] SQL parameterized queries (no string concatenation of user data)
- [x] Error messages don't expose internal stack traces to client
- [x] `college_id` always from JWT — never accepted from request body/params
- [x] Passwords excluded from all SELECT responses
- [x] Aadhaar numbers excluded from all responses
- [x] Logger uses `err.message + err.stack` (never `${err}`)
- [x] Email enumeration prevented in forgot_password (always same response)
- [x] Reset token uses `purpose` + `type` fields to prevent cross-endpoint use
- [x] `users_role_check` DB constraint covers all 6 valid roles including `tpc`

